</style>
<section class="cmp-opt" aria-labelledby="cmp-opt-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cmp-head">
      <span class="gd-eyebrow">Compare your options</span>
      <h2 id="cmp-opt-title">Removals company vs house clearance firm vs <em>Chayce</em></h2>
      <p class="cmp-intro">Three kinds of business help with a move, and they do different jobs. Here is how they compare, so you can choose the right one, or combine them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cmp-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">What you need</th><th scope="col">Removals company</th><th scope="col">House clearance firm</th><th scope="col">Chayce</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Moving belongings to a new home</th><td>Yes</td><td>No, it empties a property</td><td class="cmp-us">Yes, fully insured</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Packing</th><td>Often an extra service</td><td>No</td><td class="cmp-us">Included from Bronze Essentials</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Help deciding what to keep, sell or donate</th><td>Rarely</td><td>Rarely; items are usually cleared in bulk</td><td class="cmp-us">Yes, with your agreement, from Silver Comfort</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Emptying a property for disposal</th><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td class="cmp-us">No</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Unpacking and setting up the new home</th><td>Sometimes, at extra cost</td><td>No</td><td class="cmp-us">Included from Silver Comfort</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">One coordinator for the whole move</th><td>Not usually</td><td>No</td><td class="cmp-us">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">DBS-checked staff</th><td>Varies by company</td><td>Varies by company</td><td class="cmp-us">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Legal, financial or care advice</th><td>No</td><td>No</td><td class="cmp-us">No, we refer you to the right professional</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="cmp-note">The first two columns describe what these businesses typically offer; individual companies vary, so always ask what is included. Many families use Chayce for the sorting, packing and move, and a separate local firm for anything that needs disposing of.</p>
  </div>
</section>
